      "amount": "1/4 cup chopped",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "fresh dill",
      "amount": "1/4 cup chopped",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "lemon zest",
      "amount": "1 tablespoon",
      "notes": "use a microplane grater"
    },
    {
      "name": "kosher salt",
      "amount": "1 teaspoon",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/2 teaspoon",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "fresh thyme",
      "amount": "1/4 teaspoon dried",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "wood-fired breadcrumbs",
      "amount": "1/4 cup",
      "notes": "preferably homemade or store-bought"
    },
    {
      "name": "feta cheese",
      "amount": "1/2 cup crumbled",
      "notes": "low-sodium or reduced-fat option"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 425°F (220°C).",
    "In a large bowl, combine the minced pork, almond meal, olive oil, parsley, dill, lemon zest, salt, pepper, and thyme. Mix well with your hands until just combined.",
    "Transfer the mixture to a wood-fired baking dish or a regular oven-safe dish. Top with feta cheese and wood-fired breadcrumbs.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes, or until the top is golden brown and the internal temperature reaches 160°F (71°C).",
    "Remove from the oven and let rest for 5 minutes before slicing and serving.",
    "Garnish with additional parsley and serve immediately.",
    "This dish is best served with a side of roasted vegetables or a salad for a well-rounded meal."
  ],
